  "notice": "2026-08-03: SPEC.md sec.7 rule 5 (keep a crystallisation additive that sits within 5.0 A of the peptide, flagged) is a SPEC DEFECT, not a code bug. A glycerol/PEG/sulfate packed against the peptide is a crystallisation artefact; in solution that space is water. Keeping it docks into a pocket partly filled by something never biologically there and lets the additive be scored as receptor. Strict policy corpus-strict-hetero-1.0 supersedes it: complex.cif now holds retained protein chains + peptide + metals and monatomic ions only. The pre-correction coordinates are preserved unchanged as complex_permissive.cif / receptor_permissive.cif / complex_permissive.pdb.",
